      "writtenOn": "2022-02-09T03:35:22Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I played around with different ideas here, but it gets a little messy.\nObtaining the ptr at compile time isn\u0027t an option since it is declared\nas a pointer (and a compile time pointer assignment won\u0027t work) in shim/src/gpio.c\nSo we could keep a gpio_dt_spec as a structure and use GPIO_DT_GET_SPEC, but we run into the 32 bit flag vs 8 bit flag issue, so a custom macro would be needed.\nIt would be nice to put this into a const structure.\nAll this to avoid a single gpio_get_dt_spec() call seems a bit excessive.\nIt may be better to do some other cleanup first, before some better options\nbecome available.",
      "parentUuid": "9f64e5ef_4a439bce",
